{"case_id":"C011","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API protocol","state","configuration","input semantics","attack surface"],"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["decoder.decode_image_config?","decoder.decode_frame_config?","decoder.decode_frame?","decoder.restart_frame!","decoder.set_quirk!","decoder.frame_dirty_rect","decoder.num_decoded_frame_configs","decoder.num_decoded_frames","decoder.tell_me_more?","decoder.workbuf_len"],"reason":"H0 exclusively builds and exercises the JSON decoder, while S1 adds a JPEG image decoder implementing the base.image_decoder protocol. H0 neither enables WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JPEG nor constructs wuffs_jpeg__decoder, so JPEG byte parsing, streaming behavior, pixel-buffer/swizzler handling, and the call_sequence/restart_frame! state machine receive no fuzz coverage.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__AUX__JSON, but no JPEG module macro.","H0 calls wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson; it contains no JPEG decoder entry point.","S1 introduces pub struct decoder? implements base.image_decoder with public decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, and decode_frame? methods.","S1 parses attacker-controlled src bytes in do_decode_image_config? and returns #bad header or #truncated input based on the JPEG SOI bytes 0xFF and 0xD8.","S1 uses call_sequence values 0x00, 0x20, 0x28, 0x40, and 0x60, including restart validation through frame_config_io_position and args.src.position().","S1 decode_frame? processes caller-controlled pixel-buffer format, palette, blend, workbuf, and opts arguments and invokes swizzler.prepare! and swizzle_interleaved_from_slice!."],"recommended_action":"Add a JPEG-focused image-decoder fuzz harness that enables the JPEG module, feeds arbitrary and incrementally limited src data through decode_image_config?, decode_frame_config?, and decode_frame?, varies destination pixel formats, palettes, blend modes, and buffer boundaries, and exercises valid and invalid restart_frame! call sequences and io_position values while checking statuses, counters, dirty rectangles, and memory safety."}
